    <h1>The Viewing Fee Policy</h1>
    <p>This approved policy applies to agents and companies who choose to charge for a property viewing. Nyumba254 does not collect, hold, or guarantee viewing fees.</p>
    <p>Anyone who sets a viewing fee agrees to each clause below.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>1. Disclosure first.</strong>The fee must be visible on the listing before contact. The amount charged must equal the amount shown. A listing marked “Free viewing” must never be charged for.</li>
      <li><strong>2. Viewing only.</strong>The fee covers one viewing visit for one household at one property. It is not a booking, reservation, deposit, finder’s, commitment, agreement, administration, or key fee. No other pre-contract charge may be demanded. Any other cost must be stated in the listing description.</li>
      <li><strong>3. No gating.</strong>Contact details, price, and location must not be withheld until a fee is paid. Messaging and requesting a viewing are always free.</li>
      <li><strong>4. Payment at the viewing.</strong>The fee is paid at the property, to the person who meets the home seeker, after availability has been confirmed. Advance payment must not be required. A written or M-Pesa receipt must be issued.</li>
      <li><strong>5. Refunds.</strong>If the lister cancels, does not attend, the property is unavailable, or it is materially different from the listing, the fee must be refunded in full within 48 hours.</li>
      <li><strong>6. No price changes after confirmation.</strong>A confirmed viewing request keeps the fee shown when it was requested. The lister cannot raise that fee afterwards.</li>
      <li><strong>7. One fee per visit.</strong>Showing several units at the same property on the same visit is one fee. A repeat viewing within 14 days is free by default.</li>
      <li><strong>8. Available properties only.</strong>No viewing fee may be charged for a property that is already let, sold, or fictitious.</li>
      <li><strong>9. Honest identity.</strong>The lister must use their true role and, for companies, their registered name. Posing as an owner is prohibited.</li>
      <li><strong>10. Maximum.</strong>The platform viewing-fee cap applies. Fees above the current cap are blocked by the system.</li>
      <li><strong>11. No pressure or threats.</strong>Harassment, intimidation, and linking the fee to signing anything are prohibited.</li>
      <li><strong>12. Cooperation.</strong>Listers must keep receipts and respond to viewing-fee disputes within three working days.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Reports and enforcement</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Valid report.</strong>A valid report may result in a warning and a request for evidence.</li>
      <li><strong>Repeated reports.</strong>Two valid reports within 90 days may freeze the lister’s viewing-fee privilege. Their listings will show as free while that privilege is paused.</li>
      <li><strong>Serious or repeated breaches.</strong>Serious or repeated breaches may result in listings being hidden and, where warranted, account suspension.</li>
      <li><strong>Platform role.</strong>Nyumba254 does not collect or guarantee viewing fees. Fee disputes are handled through reporting and moderation; Nyumba254 does not mediate payments or refunds.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Fee amounts are paid directly to the person conducting the viewing. Never pay rent, a deposit, or another charge before viewing the property in person.</p>
